The official CPU library also contains LIBSVM by Chih-Chung Chang and Chih-Jen
Lin. Its separate terms are reproduced in licenses/LIBSVM.txt.

The optional CUDA build uses the CUDA Toolkit's CUB radix-sort headers.
The notices of the tested CUDA 13.0 headers are in licenses/NVIDIA-CUB.txt;
the actual toolkit's terms also apply when building with another version.

Adapted source files retain their upstream copyright notices and license.
The CUDA source manifest identifies the original files and their SHA-256 hashes.
The owned integration code is covered by the repository's MIT license.

The executable links the official CPU libvmaf for model prediction and pooling,
and uses FFmpeg libraries for decoding and pixel conversion. Their licenses and
the licenses of enabled components still apply to any binary distribution.
NVIDIA CUDA and the Vulkan SDK/runtime are external build/runtime dependencies;
their vendor terms apply independently. This source tree does not bundle them.
